{
  "title": "Fail finalization when required game artifacts cannot be read or \
written",
  "description": "game_finalization silently ignores OSError while reading or \
appending game_events.jsonl and while reading per-player error logs. \
write_error_log can consequently write 'No errors detected.' even when an \
error log was unreadable, and ensure_game_over_event can fabricate or fail to \
persist a terminal event without surfacing the failure. These artifacts feed \
exports, blunder analysis, and the leaderboard, so silent degradation can \
publish misleading data. Define which finalization artifacts are required, \
propagate failures with the affected path, and prevent website export when \
they cannot be read or written. If any artifact is intentionally optional, \
record an explicit structured finalization error rather than treating it as \
absent. Add permission/read-error/write-error tests.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "orchestration",
    "logging",
    "data-integrity",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-11T11:32:21.127-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-07-11T11:32:21.127-07:00",
}
